  "term": "RN",
  "definition": "An RN is a nurse who completes an approved nursing education program, qualifies through a state licensing examination, and is authorized by a state body to practice nursing. Training for this role can come from diploma, associate-level, or bachelor’s-level nursing pathways, including mixed routes.",
